Subject: [PATCH 14/40] tei-v7 struct-18: Issue-to-diff semantic traceability
 gate

---
 evaluation/patch_selection/trae_selector/selector_agent.py | 3 ++-
 tei/candidates.jsonl                                       | 1 +
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/evaluation/patch_selection/trae_selector/selector_agent.py b/evaluation/patch_selection/trae_selector/selector_agent.py
index 343b498..9868ddc 100755
--- a/evaluation/patch_selection/trae_selector/selector_agent.py
+++ b/evaluation/patch_selection/trae_selector/selector_agent.py
@@ -24,7 +24,8 @@ class CandidatePatch:
 def build_system_prompt(candidate_length: int) -> str:
     init_prompt = f"""\
 Before judging a candidate, classify every failure as environment/setup, patch-application, assertion mismatch, exception mismatch, or unrelated regression. For assertion or exception failures, require a minimal reproducer and one targeted follow-up experiment before accepting or rejecting the patch. Escalate from focused test to related test module to broader regression tests only when the narrower result is insufficient.
-# ROLE: Act as an expert code evaluator. Given a codebase, a GitHub issue, and **{candidate_length} candidate patches** proposed by your colleagues, select the patch that actually solves the issue.
+# ROLE: Act as an expert code evaluator.
+For each candidate, construct an issue-to-diff trace: map every changed hunk to a requirement or discovered invariant, identify the runtime path it affects, and explain why unchanged neighboring paths remain safe. Prefer the smallest coherent patch; reject candidates that pass a narrow test but contain unrelated edits, speculative refactors, or no demonstrated coverage of the reported failure. Given a codebase, a GitHub issue, and **{candidate_length} candidate patches** proposed by your colleagues, select the patch that actually solves the issue.
 
 # EVIDENCE GATE:
 Reject patches that are merely plausible. First verify that the candidate changes the implementation path identified by the issue, then require a focused reproducer or test demonstrating the requested behavior, relevant regression coverage, and consistency with existing public API and error semantics. Penalize broad unrelated edits, tests that do not exercise the changed path, and patches whose explanation does not account for alternate implementations or subclasses.ence, regression evidence, and a clear explanation of why the failing behavior changes without breaking neighboring behavior. If evidence is missing, inspect the repository and run the smallest decisive test before selecting.
diff --git a/tei/candidates.jsonl b/tei/candidates.jsonl
index 7b5a2e3..7570b0f 100644
--- a/tei/candidates.jsonl
+++ b/tei/candidates.jsonl
@@ -14,3 +14,4 @@
